\tag{fdip}
\title{States and conditional expectations}
\date{2026-11-02}

\p{Can the physics be rebuilt from its observables alone? This chapter asks how
a state on a finite-dimensional algebra determines a Hilbert space.}

\p{The first section builds that space from the Gram form #{\omega(a^*b)}.
Its dimension is the rank of the Gram matrix. On a direct sum of matrix
algebras that rank is the sum of each block size times the rank of the
density, and on functions the space is #{\ell^2} of the support. No norm
on the algebra is assumed. The following section takes up conditional
expectations.}

